{
  "id": "extension-reflex",
  "term": "extension reflex",
  "definition": "In this context, the extension reflex refers to the proboscis extension reflex: an insect’s automatic extension of the proboscis when taste receptors contact an appealing substance such as sugar. It is used in learning research as an observable measure of how the insect detects and responds to tastants, including changes with habituation and memory.",
